   "_dt": 1793640565.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "ABUJA — President Bola Tinubu has concluded his visit to Saudi Arabia, where he performed the Umrah pilgrimage and entered the Holy Kaaba to pray. Tinubu, who departed Abuja last Thursday, announced the conclusion of his visit on Monday in a post on his X account. He said the visit reflected the longstanding bonds of faith and friendship between Nigeria and Saudi Arabia.",
   "summary_zh": "阿布贾——博拉·蒂努布总统结束了对沙特的访问，期间他完成了副朝觐，并进入天房祈祷。蒂努布于上周四离开阿布贾，周一发帖宣布此次访问结束。他说，此行体现了尼日利亚与沙特之间由来已久的信仰和友谊纽带。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "ABUJA — President Bola Tinubu has concluded his visit to Saudi Arabia, where he performed the Umrah pilgrimage and entered the Holy Kaaba to pray. Tinubu, who departed Abuja last Thursday, announced the conclusion of his visit on Monday in a post on his X account. The President was accompanied on the trip by some state governors, members of the business community and cabinet ministers. In the post, Tinubu said he and members of his delegation had the rare privilege of entering the Holy Kaaba to pray and performing Umrah. He expressed gratitude to the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques, King Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud, and the Crown Prince and Prime Minister, Mohammed bin Salman, for granting them the privilege and extending hospitality to the delegation. He said the visit reflected the longstanding bonds of faith and friendship between Nigeria and Saudi Arabia. Tinubu added that he used the opportunity to pray for peace, unity and prosperity for Nigeria and its citizens. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
