   "title": "Audit Service recovers over GH¢18bn in public funds since 2022 and 2026",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/audit-service-recovers-over-gh%c2%a218bn-in-public-funds-since-2022-and-2026-auditor-general/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:18:56 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793639936.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "The Auditor-General, Dr Pamela Graham, said the Audit Service recovered more than GH¢18 billion in public funds between 2022 and 2026 through its audit activities. According to her, the Audit Service also helped save the country GH¢11.7 billion in 2025 alone by identifying and preventing wrongful payments.",
   "summary_zh": "审计长帕梅拉·格雷厄姆博士表示，审计署通过开展审计工作，在2022年至2026年期间追回了超过GH¢180亿公款。据她介绍，审计署仅在2025年就通过识别并阻止不当支付，为国家节省了GH¢117亿。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Auditor-General, Dr Pamela Graham, said the Audit Service recovered more than GH¢18 billion in public funds between 2022 and 2026 through its audit activities. According to her, the Audit Service also helped save the country GH¢11.7 billion in 2025 alone by identifying and preventing wrongful payments. Speaking at the African Organisation of Public Accounts Committees Conference, Dr Graham said there was a need for public institutions to implement corrective measures based on audit findings to strengthen accountability and improve the management of public funds. She explained that audit reports should go beyond merely identifying financial irregularities after they occur and instead serve as a basis for strengthening internal controls and informing policy formulation. “From 2022 to date, we have actually recovered over 18 billion Ghana cedis from the work of the Auditor-General. We have saved the country about 11.7 billion from wrongful payments only in just in 2025,” she said. Dr Graham said the impact of auditing should not be measured solely by the identification of financial irregularities, but also by how effectively institutions use audit findings to prevent similar occurrences. She noted that translating audit findings into policy and institutional reforms would help strengthen governance, improve accountability and ensure the prudent use of public resources. The Auditor-General therefore called for greater attention to the implementation of audit recommendations, stressing that the information generated through financial audits could play a critical role in improving public sector management and preventing future losses",
