   "title": "Doval meets Vietnam Defence Minister, agrees to deepen bilateral defence cooperation",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/doval-meets-vietnam-defence-minister-agrees-to-deepen-bilateral-defence-cooperation/article71655993.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:47:54 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793639874.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription National Security Adviser (NSA) Ajit Doval on Monday (November 2, 2026) held discussions with Vietnam’s Deputy Prime Minister and Defence Minister, General Phan Van Giang, in Hanoi, reviewing the progress of bilateral defence cooperation and agreeing to further deepen engagement in the sector. The Embassy of India in Vietnam, in a post on X, said the two leaders reviewed ongoing defence cooperation and explored ways to expand engagement.",
   "summary_zh": "解锁这些内容需订阅。国家安全顾问（NSA）阿吉特·多瓦尔于11月2日星期一在河内与越南副总理兼国防部长范潘·江大将举行会谈，审议双边防务合作进展，并同意进一步深化该领域的接触。印度驻越南大使馆在X上发文称，两国领导人审议了正在开展的防务合作，并探讨了扩大接触的方式。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription National Security Adviser (NSA) Ajit Doval on Monday (November 2, 2026) held discussions with Vietnam’s Deputy Prime Minister and Defence Minister, General Phan Van Giang, in Hanoi, reviewing the progress of bilateral defence cooperation and agreeing to further deepen engagement in the sector. The meeting was part of Mr. Doval’s two-day official visit to Vietnam, aimed at strengthening the India-Vietnam Enhanced Comprehensive Strategic Partnership. The Embassy of India in Vietnam, in a post on X, said the two leaders reviewed ongoing defence cooperation and explored ways to expand engagement. Mr. Doval arrived in Hanoi on Sunday and is scheduled to interact with senior Vietnamese leadership to discuss cooperation in security, defence and strategic affairs. The visit follows the fourth India-Vietnam Security Dialogue held in New Delhi in October 2026, during which both sides reviewed cooperation in counter-terrorism, cybersecurity, maritime security, economic security and emerging technologies. Mr. Doval’s visit is expected to provide high-level political direction to the implementation of the outcomes of the dialogue. Vietnam remains an important strategic partner for India under its Act East Policy and broader Indo-Pacific vision. Both countries have also emphasised the importance of maintaining peace, stability and freedom of navigation in the Indo-Pacific region. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
