   "_dt": 1793443770.0,
   "ageDays": 2.32,
   "summary": "The state government, during the exercise led by the wife of Lagos State Governor, Dr Ibijoke Sanwo-Olu, in the Ajina area of Ikorodu Local Government, and the Head of Service, Mr Bode Agoro, in the Ikeja area of the state, warned that the practice undermines sanitation efforts and increases the risk of flooding. He stressed that sanitation must be a continuous responsibility, noting that government officials observed residents dumping refuse into canals during the exercise.",
   "summary_zh": "在该州政府开展行动期间，拉各斯州州长夫人伊比乔克·桑沃奥卢博士在伊科罗杜地方政府的阿吉纳地区带队，州政府首席幕僚博德·阿戈罗先生则在伊凯贾地区带队；他们警告称，这种行为会削弱卫生工作成效，并增加发生洪水的风险。他强调，卫生工作必须持续落实；行动期间，政府官员发现居民向运河倾倒垃圾。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The state government, during the exercise led by the wife of Lagos State Governor, Dr Ibijoke Sanwo-Olu, in the Ajina area of Ikorodu Local Government, and the Head of Service, Mr Bode Agoro, in the Ikeja area of the state, warned that the practice undermines sanitation efforts and increases the risk of flooding. The wife of the Lagos State Governor, Dr Ibijoke Sanwo-Olu, disclosed this while monitoring the monthly environmental sanitation exercise in Ikorodu. The governor’s wife urged residents of Ikorodu to sustain the exercise beyond the last Saturday of every month and work towards emerging as the cleanest Local Government Area in the state. She emphasised that continuous public sensitisation remains essential for promoting environmental cleanliness, despite the challenges of behavioural change. Mrs Sanwo-Olu encouraged residents to embrace proper sanitation practices in their homes, schools, markets and communities, stressing that keeping Lagos clean is a collective responsibility. She commended the active participation of residents, particularly children, youths, market traders and environmental sanitation workers, who turned out early to clean their surroundings. In the same vein, Agoro said the exercise was the seventh since March, calling on local government chairpersons and their executives to mobilise residents to improve environmental cleanliness. He stressed that sanitation must be a continuous responsibility, noting that government officials observed residents dumping refuse into canals during the exercise. According to him, the Ministry of the Environment has been notified to clear affected canals, while plans are also underway to reconstruct a canal in the area in consultation with the relevant drainage authorities. Agoro, however, cautioned that clearing the canals would achieve little if residents continued to dispose of waste indiscriminately. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
