   "title": "8. ZAMFARA STATE: POLICE/MILITARY OPERATION LAUNCHES RESCUE EFFORT FOR NINE ABDUCTED PERSONS ✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 0600HRS, armed bandits",
   "url": "https://x.com/PoliceNG/status/2116818487637135588",
   "snippet": "8. ZAMFARA STATE: POLICE/MILITARY OPERATION LAUNCHES RESCUE EFFORT FOR NINE ABDUCTED PERSONS\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 0600HRS, armed bandits invaded the Upa area on the outskirts of Kurya Madaro, Kaura Namoda LGA, and abducted nine persons.\n✅ Police VCRU teams and military personnel under Operation Fansar Yamma were immediately mobilized to the scene.\n✅ Combined bush-combing operations are ongoing across surrounding forests to rescue the victims and apprehend the perpetrators.\n🔹 Status: SCID Gusau Investigating.\n\n9. BENUE STATE: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS IN DEFILEMENT CASE\n✅ Following a report of the alleged defilement of a 16-year-old female at Naka, Gwer West LGA, police operatives arrested two alleged accomplices.\n✅ The victim was taken to General Hospital Naka, where medical examination confirmed penetration.\n✅ Efforts are ongoing to apprehend the principal suspect, who remains at large.\n🔹 Status: SCID Makurdi Investigating.\n\n10. FCT ABUJA: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS OVER GRIEVOUS HURT\n✅ On 29/10/2026, an argument over a snatched Tecno mobile phone escalated into a group fight in Gwagwalada.\n✅ A passer-by, Zaharadenu Awalu, 19, sustained a severe cut injury to his left hand and was treated at UATH.\n✅ Police operatives arrested Mensur Abdullahi, 20, and Gambo Salisu, 30, while efforts continue to apprehend fleeing accomplices.\n🔹 Status: CID Abuja Investigating.\n\n11. ANAMBRA STATE: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS OVER DEATH IN VIGILANTE CUSTODY\n✅ Following a report that a suspect accused of stealing a vehicle battery was allegedly tortured and detained overnight by vigilante members at Odorober, Odekpe, resulting in his death, police operatives visited the scene.\n✅ The operatives processed the scene and arrested two suspects, while efforts are ongoing to apprehend another suspect who remains at large.\n🔹 Status: SCID Awka Investigating.\n\nCSP ANI INIEDU, anipr\nFORCE PUBLIC RELATIONS OFFICE\nFORCE HEADQUARTERS\nABUJA",
   "body": "8. ZAMFARA STATE: POLICE/MILITARY OPERATION LAUNCHES RESCUE EFFORT FOR NINE ABDUCTED PERSONS\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 0600HRS, armed bandits invaded the Upa area on the outskirts of Kurya Madaro, Kaura Namoda LGA, and abducted nine persons.\n✅ Police VCRU teams and military personnel under Operation Fansar Yamma were immediately mobilized to the scene.\n✅ Combined bush-combing operations are ongoing across surrounding forests to rescue the victims and apprehend the perpetrators.\n🔹 Status: SCID Gusau Investigating.\n\n9. BENUE STATE: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS IN DEFILEMENT CASE\n✅ Following a report of the alleged defilement of a 16-year-old female at Naka, Gwer West LGA, police operatives arrested two alleged accomplices.\n✅ The victim was taken to General Hospital Naka, where medical examination confirmed penetration.\n✅ Efforts are ongoing to apprehend the principal suspect, who remains at large.\n🔹 Status: SCID Makurdi Investigating.\n\n10. FCT ABUJA: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS OVER GRIEVOUS HURT\n✅ On 29/10/2026, an argument over a snatched Tecno mobile phone escalated into a group fight in Gwagwalada.\n✅ A passer-by, Zaharadenu Awalu, 19, sustained a severe cut injury to his left hand and was treated at UATH.\n✅ Police operatives arrested Mensur Abdullahi, 20, and Gambo Salisu, 30, while efforts continue to apprehend fleeing accomplices.\n🔹 Status: CID Abuja Investigating.\n\n11. ANAMBRA STATE: POLICE ARREST TWO SUSPECTS OVER DEATH IN VIGILANTE CUSTODY\n✅ Following a report that a suspect accused of stealing a vehicle battery was allegedly tortured and detained overnight by vigilante members at Odorober, Odekpe, resulting in his death, police operatives visited the scene.\n✅ The operatives processed the scene and arrested two suspects, while efforts are ongoing to apprehend another suspect who remains at large.\n🔹 Status: SCID Awka Investigating.\n\nCSP ANI INIEDU, anipr\nFORCE PUBLIC RELATIONS OFFICE\nFORCE HEADQUARTERS\nABUJA",
